    {
      "id": "release-graph-landing",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Release Graph landing",
      "position": {
        "x": 50,
        "y": -1387
      },
      "width": 633.5114535153646,
      "height": 270.2697209374306,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "visible": false,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "release-graph"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Release Graph\n\nA release is a graph with one **release date**, a title and a few **entries**. Each entry is a Release Entry card: a title, a category (new, changed or fixed) and a summary for a customer.\n\nThe Detail, Summary, Glyph and the poster behind the entries are not written by hand: the Method reads the graph and writes them. The intro under the title is the root's description, the date is its `releaseDate`, and the highlights are the titles of the entries in New, so none of them is typed twice. The poster has a lane for each category: put an entry in its lane.\n\nA graph made from this template **imports it once** (an import of this template's graph), and gets the Release Entry class and the Method. Set the graph's name, description and `releaseDate` (as YYYY-MM-DD) on its root. To link the poster to the release before it and to the archive it belongs to, set `previousRelease` and `archive` (addresses) there too.\n\nA published release is not edited: a correction is a new release."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "release-graph-derive-method",
      "type": "method",
      "label": "Assemble the release",
      "position": {
        "x": -50,
        "y": 1233
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180,
          "portId": "call"
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0,
          "portId": "result"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "scriptName": "Assemble the release",
        "parameters": [],
        "source": "// Derives a release's views from its entries: nothing is typed into a view.\n// It reads the release's own identity (its name, its description, its release date, and optionally the address of the release before it and of the archive it belongs to) and the Release Entry cards (nodes of the\n// type `release-entry`), in the order they sit in the graph. It writes the Detail (the release as a page: a masthead, the highlights, and the entries under New, Changed and Fixed), the Summary (a card: the date and\n// the three counts), the Glyph and the environment (the poster: the date as its title, the intro, the links to the previous release and the archive, and a lane for each category), and only those, which its declared\n// effects say. The intro is the root's description, the date its release date and the highlights the titles of the entries in New, so none is typed twice. A card with a review record (a private one, from the queue)\n// is not published here, so it is left out: the page shows public fields only. The lanes are where the cards go; the cards are placed in them by whoever makes the release (scripts/library/releaseLanes.mjs holds the\n// numbers, and a test holds this poster to them).\nconst clean = (value) => String(value ?? '').trim();\nconst esc = (value) => clean(value).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');\nconst SERIF = 'Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Georgia,serif'; const SANS = 'Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif'; const MONO = 'ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace';\nconst VIOLET = '#354B58'; const GOLD = '#b45309'; const SUN = '#B18649'; const INK = '#292D2C'; const PAPER = '#F4F0E6'; const MUTED = '#64748b';\nconst CATEGORIES = [['new', 'New', '#15803d', 'rgba(21,128,61,.09)'], ['changed', 'Changed', '#1d4ed8', 'rgba(29,78,216,.09)'], ['fixed', 'Fixed', '#b45309', 'rgba(180,83,9,.09)']];\nconst MONTHS = ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', 'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'];\n// The stage of the poster, in cqw of the window's width (the same numbers as scripts/library/releaseLanes.mjs).\nconst STAGE = { left: 4, right: 4, top: 21, bottom: 6 }; const LANE_GAP = 2.5;\nconst LANE_WIDTH = (100 - STAGE.left - STAGE.right - LANE_GAP * (CATEGORIES.length - 1)) / CATEGORIES.length;\n// A lane is as tall as the fullest one needs: its label, the rows of cards (two across, never fewer than two rows) and a little room (the same numbers as releaseLanes.mjs, in graph units; 45 to the cqw).\nconst LANE_LABEL = 170; const CARD_HEIGHT = 300; const CARD_GAP = 60; const LANE_PAD = 40; const UNIT = 45;\n\nconst nodes = await api.getNodes();\n// A graph that borrows this Method from its template declares its own writes. The newer surfaces (the Icon and, where the template did not write one before, the\n// environment) are written only where that declaration names them, so an older graph keeps what it has and is not refused.\nconst declaredHere = (target) => Boolean(target) && nodes.some((method) => method.type === 'method' && (method.data?.effects || []).some((effect) => effect.kind === 'update-node' && (!effect.targets || effect.targets.includes(target.id))));\nconst edges = await api.getEdges();\nconst root = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'root');\nconst identity = root?.data?.identity || {};\nconst name = clean(identity.name) || 'A release';\nconst lead = clean(identity.description);\nconst previous = clean(identity.previousRelease);\nconst archive = clean(identity.archive);\nconst dateParts = /^(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})$/.exec(clean(identity.releaseDate));\nconst month = dateParts ? MONTHS[Number(dateParts[2]) - 1] : '';\nconst dateText = dateParts && month ? `${Number(dateParts[3])} ${month} ${dateParts[1]}` : '';\nconst dateShort = dateParts && month ? `${Number(dateParts[3])} ${month.slice(0, 3)} ${dateParts[1]}` : '';\nconst entries = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'release-entry' && !(node.data && node.data.review));\nconst titleOf = (entry) => clean(entry.data?.title || entry.label) || 'Untitled';\nconst inCategory = (key) => entries.filter((entry) => clean(entry.data?.category) === key);\nconst highlights = inCategory('new').slice(0, 3);\nconst counts = CATEGORIES.map(([key]) => inCategory(key).length);\nconst plural = (n, one, many) => `${n} ${n === 1 ? one : many}`;\n\nconst paragraphs = (text, size) => clean(text).split(/\\n{2,}/).map((p) => p.trim()).filter(Boolean)\n  .map((p) => `<div style='font:400 ${size}cqw/1.55 ${SERIF};color:#334155;margin-top:.6cqw'>${esc(p)}</div>`).join('');\nconst heading = (label, colour, count) => `<div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;margin:4cqw 0 1.6cqw;padding-top:2cqw;border-top:.15cqw solid rgba(53,75,88,.35)'>`\n  + `<span style='font:700 1.5cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${colour}'>${label}</span>`\n  + `<span style='font:600 1.4cqw/1 ${SANS};color:${MUTED}'>${count}</span></div>`;\nconst entryBlock = (entry, colour) => `<div style='margin-bottom:2.4cqw;padding:2.2cqw 2.6cqw;border-radius:0;background:#FCF9F1;border:1px solid #D4CABB;border-left:.7cqw solid ${colour}'>`\n  + `<div style='font:850 3.1cqw/1.2 ${SANS};color:${INK}'>${esc(titleOf(entry))}</div>`\n  + paragraphs(entry.data?.summary, 2.5)\n  + paragraphs(entry.data?.detail, 2.1)\n  + (clean(entry.data?.ref) ? `<div style='margin-top:1cqw;font:600 1.5cqw/1.4 ${SANS};color:${VIOLET};overflow-wrap:anywhere'>${esc(entry.data.ref)}</div>` : '')\n  + `</div>`;\n\n// ---- the Detail: the release as a page\nconst detail = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:${PAPER};font-family:${SERIF};color:${INK}'>`\n  + `<div style='box-sizing:border-box;min-height:100%;padding:4.4cqw 7cqw 5cqw'>`\n  + `<div style='padding:1.4cqw 0;border-top:.4cqw solid ${INK};border-bottom:.1cqw solid ${INK};display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:700 1.3cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${VIOLET}'><span>Release notes</span><span style='color:${GOLD}'>${esc(dateText)}</span></div>`\n  + `<div style='font:850 8.2cqw/1.02 ${SANS};letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:3cqw 0 .8cqw;color:${INK}'>${esc(name)}</div>`\n  + (lead ? `<div style='font:400 2.2cqw/1.5 ${SERIF};color:#334155;margin-top:2cqw;max-width:62cqw'>${esc(lead)}</div>` : '')\n  + (highlights.length ? `<div style='margin-top:3cqw'><div style='font:700 1.3cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${GOLD};margin-bottom:1.2cqw'>Highlights</div>`\n    + highlights.map((entry) => `<div style='font:600 1.9cqw/1.5 ${SANS};color:${INK};margin-top:.5cqw'><span style='color:${GOLD}'>◆</span> ${esc(titleOf(entry))}</div>`).join('') + `</div>` : '')\n  + (entries.length ? CATEGORIES.map(([key, label, colour]) => (inCategory(key).length ? heading(label, colour, plural(inCategory(key).length, 'change', 'changes')) + inCategory(key).map((entry) => entryBlock(entry, colour)).join('') : '')).join('')\n    : `<div style='margin-top:4cqw;font:italic 1.8cqw/1.5 ${SERIF};color:${MUTED}'>No entries yet.</div>`)\n  + `</div></div>`;\n\n// ---- the Summary: the date, and the three counts\nconst column = ([, label, colour], count) => `<div style='flex:1;min-width:0;text-align:center;border-top:1cqw solid ${count ? colour : '#cbd5e1'};padding-top:1.6cqw'>`\n  + `<div style='font:700 13cqw/1 ${SERIF};color:${count ? colour : '#cbd5e1'}'>${count}</div>`\n  + `<div style='font:750 4.6cqw/1.2 ${SANS};color:${count ? colour : MUTED};margin-top:1cqw'>${label}</div></div>`;\nconst summary = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:6cqw 7cqw 5cqw;border-radius:0;background:${PAPER};border:1px solid #C8BFB0;border-top:1.8cqw solid ${VIOLET};color:${INK};overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3cqw'>`\n  + `<div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2cqw;font:700 3cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${VIOLET};white-space:nowrap'><span>Release notes</span><span style='color:${GOLD}'>${esc(dateShort)}</span></div>`\n  + (`<div style='font:850 7.2cqw/1.05 ${SANS};display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden'>${esc(name)}</div>`)\n  + `<div style='display:flex;gap:3cqw;flex:1;min-height:0'>${CATEGORIES.map((category, i) => column(category, counts[i])).join('')}</div>`\n  + (highlights.length ? `<div style='font:500 3.4cqw/1.3 ${SANS};color:${MUTED};white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'><span style='color:${GOLD}'>◆</span> ${esc(titleOf(highlights[0]))}</div>` : '')\n  + `</div></div>`;\n\nconst icon = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:${PAPER};color:${INK};padding:4cqw;border-top:1.5cqw solid ${VIOLET};display:flex;flex-direction:column;overflow:hidden'><div style='border-bottom:1px solid ${INK};padding-bottom:1cqw;font:800 4.5cqw/1.2 ${SANS};letter-spacing:.12em'>RELEASE NOTES · ${esc(dateShort)}</div><div style='display:flex;align-items:center;flex:1;min-height:0;gap:3cqw'><div style='flex:1;font:850 8cqw/1.05 ${SANS};overflow-wrap:anywhere;display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden'>${esc(name)}</div><div style='width:29cqw;flex:none'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 120 120' width='100%' height='100%'><rect width='120' height='120' fill='#354B58'/><path d='M17 19h86v82H17Z' fill='#F4F0E6'/><path d='M27 31h66v8H27ZM27 49h66M27 58h66M27 70h30M27 80h30M27 90h30' stroke='#354B58' stroke-width='4'/><path d='M67 69h26v22H67Z' fill='#B18649'/></svg></div></div><div style='border-top:1px solid ${INK};padding-top:1cqw;font:750 4.2cqw/1.2 ${SANS};color:${VIOLET}'>${entries.length} changes</div></div></div>`;\n// ---- the poster: the environment the entries stand on. The date is its title; each category has a lane.\nconst laneRows = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(Math.max(...counts) / 2));\nconst laneHeight = (LANE_LABEL + laneRows * (CARD_HEIGHT + CARD_GAP) - CARD_GAP + LANE_PAD) / UNIT;\nconst lane = ([, label, colour, tint], i, count) => `<div style='position:absolute;left:${STAGE.left + i * (LANE_WIDTH + LANE_GAP)}cqw;top:${STAGE.top}cqw;width:${LANE_WIDTH}cqw;height:${laneHeight}cqw;box-sizing:border-box;border-radius:0;background:${tint};border-top:.5cqw solid ${colour}'>`\n  + `<div style='position:absolute;left:1.4cqw;top:1cqw;font:700 1.15cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${colour}'>${label} · ${count}</div></div>`;\nconst link = (href, text) => `<a href='${esc(href)}' style='color:${VIOLET};text-decoration:none'>${text}</a>`;\nconst poster = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:linear-gradient(160deg,${PAPER},#E5DED0);font-family:${SERIF};color:${INK}'>`\n  + `<div style='position:absolute;inset:0;background-image:repeating-linear-gradient(0deg,rgba(53,75,88,.06) 0,rgba(53,75,88,.06) .12cqw,transparent .12cqw,transparent 4.2cqw)'></div>`\n  + `<div style='position:absolute;inset:1.4cqw;border:.2cqw solid rgba(53,75,88,.5)'></div>`\n  + `<div style='position:absolute;left:1.4cqw;right:1.4cqw;top:1.4cqw;height:.9cqw;background:${SUN}'></div>`\n  + `<div style='position:absolute;left:4.6cqw;top:3.8cqw;font:700 1.3cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${VIOLET}'>Release notes</div>`\n  + `<div style='position:absolute;left:4.6cqw;right:30cqw;top:6.2cqw;font:850 5.8cqw/1.05 ${SANS};color:${INK};white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${esc(dateText || name)}</div>`\n  + (lead ? `<div style='position:absolute;left:4.6cqw;right:30cqw;top:13.2cqw;font:italic 1.9cqw/1.35 ${SERIF};color:${MUTED};display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden'>${esc(lead)}</div>` : '')\n  + ((previous || archive) ? `<div style='position:absolute;right:4.6cqw;top:4cqw;text-align:right;font:600 1.6cqw/1.7 ${SANS}'>${previous ? link(previous, '← Previous release') : ''}${previous && archive ? '<br>' : ''}${archive ? link(archive, 'The archive →') : ''}</div>` : '')\n  + CATEGORIES.map((category, i) => lane(category, i, counts[i])).join('')\n  + `</div></div>`;\n\n// ---- write them\nconst faces = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'face');\nconst faceFor = (level) => faces.find((node) => clean(node.data?.semanticLevel) === level);\nconst environmentEdge = edges.find((edge) => clean(edge.type) === 'environment' && edge.source === root?.id);\nconst environment = environmentEdge ? nodes.find((node) => node.id === environmentEdge.target) : null;\nconst glyph = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'glyph');\nfor (const [target, html] of [[faceFor('detail'), detail], [faceFor('summary'), summary], [declaredHere(faceFor('icon')) ? faceFor('icon') : undefined, icon], [environment, poster]]) {\n  if (target) await api.updateView(target.id, { content: { kind: 'html', value: html } });\n}\nif (glyph) await api.updateNode(glyph.id, { data: { ...glyph.data, glyph: {\"kind\":\"svg\",\"value\":\"<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 120 120' width='100%' height='100%'><rect width='120' height='120' fill='#354B58'/><path d='M17 19h86v82H17Z' fill='#F4F0E6'/><path d='M27 31h66v8H27ZM27 49h66M27 58h66M27 70h30M27 80h30M27 90h30' stroke='#354B58' stroke-width='4'/><path d='M67 69h26v22H67Z' fill='#B18649'/></svg>\",\"color\":\"#354B58\"} } });\nreturn { name, date: clean(identity.releaseDate), entries: entries.length, new: counts[0], changed: counts[1], fixed: counts[2] };\n",
        "effects": [
          {
            "kind": "update-node",
            "targets": [
              "release-graph-detail",
              "release-graph-summary",
              "release-graph-glyph",
              "release-graph-environment",
              "release-graph-icon"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "allowMutations": true,
        "dryRun": false,
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "release-graph-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "release-graph-export",
      "type": "export",
      "label": "Release Graph (Export)",
      "position": {
